{
  "passage": "Leo, 16, helps his elderly neighbour Mr. Davies every Saturday morning. Mr. Davies used to be a keen cyclist, but an accident means he can't ride his bike anymore. Now, he spends his time writing his life story. Last week, Mr. Davies asked Leo for help with his new computer. 'I need to provide a clear description of my old adventures for my book,' he explained. 'But I'm not good with the keyboard.' Leo happily agreed. He showed Mr. Davies how to type and save his files. Mr. Davies writes about his cycling tours and the interesting characters he met. He has a fantastic vocabulary for describing places. To thank Leo, Mr. Davies gave him a cheque for his birthday. Leo was surprised and grateful. He feels good about using his computer skills to help someone share their amazing stories with the world.",
